# Chip atlas data: every value typed in by hand from the source named next to it (all fetched 2026-10-05).
# Run: python3 chips_data.py  -> writes chips.json and ../parts/31_js_chips_0data.js
# Conventions:
#   peaks: TFLOPS (TOPS for int8) per chip, DENSE (no 2:4 structured sparsity). "sp" holds the vendor's sparse figure when printed.
#   bw: memory bandwidth in TB/s per chip; mem: GB (decimal) per chip; GiB values converted and said so in the note.
#   link: scale-up link bandwidth per chip in GB/s as the vendor prints it (NVIDIA, AMD and Google: bidirectional total).
#   Every field that is derived (divided from a rack figure, converted from GiB) says so in "d" (derivations).
